Global PC SSD market size was valued at USD 18,053 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 24,741 million by 2034, exhibiting a CAGR of 4.7% during the forecast period.
A PC Solid State Drive (PC SSD) is a non‑volatile storage device that employs NAND flash memory together with a controller chip for data management. It serves desktops and laptops as a high‑speed alternative to hard‑disk drives, connecting via PCIe or SATA interfaces and delivering low latency, shock resistance, and reduced power consumption.
